@startuml
title T12-WF03 — AI Lead Scoring Agent (Sequence)
autonumber
participant "RabbitMQ" as MQ
participant "n8n WF03\nLead Scoring" as N8N
participant "NestJS Backend" as API
database "PostgreSQL" as DB
participant "Scoring Policy Service\ninside NestJS" as POLICY

MQ -> N8N: lead.scoring.requested(eventId, leadId)
activate N8N
N8N -> N8N: Validate event, correlation and idempotency IDs
N8N -> API: GET lead profile
API -> DB: Read lead
DB --> API: Lead data
API --> N8N: Lead profile
N8N -> API: GET latest qualification
API -> DB: Read qualification history
DB --> API: Latest qualification or empty result
API --> N8N: Qualification
N8N -> API: GET latest enrichment and interactions
API -> DB: Read enrichment + interaction signals
DB --> API: Available signals
API --> N8N: Context (missing sources explicit)
N8N -> N8N: Aggregate deterministic scoring features
N8N -> API: POST scoring evaluation request
API -> POLICY: Evaluate features using versioned policy
POLICY --> API: Canonical score, label, policyVersion
API --> N8N: Canonical score response
N8N -> N8N: Validate score bounds, label and policy version
N8N -> API: POST score callback
API -> DB: Persist score history idempotently
DB --> API: Score record ID
API --> N8N: Persisted result
alt Lead crosses agreed high-priority threshold
N8N -> API: Request next-action suggestion/notification
API -> DB: Persist suggestion or notification audit
API --> N8N: Accepted
else Normal priority
N8N -> N8N: Finalize scoring output without hot-lead notification
end
deactivate N8N
note over N8N,POLICY
NestJS owns the canonical score and threshold policy. n8n must not
independently calculate a conflicting official score.
end note
@enduml
